{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b1f86766418dbbe6","name":"card_unit_dinah_iii","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Breakthrough/units/card_unit_dinah_iii","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"Ki-46 DINAH III","text":"Deployment: Draw two random 1-cost units from your deck.","flavorText":"The Mitsubishi Ki-46, Allied code name “Dinah”,  was a Japanese twin engined reconnaissance aircraft used by the Imperial Japanese Army and Navy air forces during WWII. The aircraft came into service in 1941 and was used before and during the Pacific War, mostly for reconnaissance missions. The Ki-46 was considered a difficult aircraft to counter and only a few were intercepted by Allied pilots. Between 1944-45 a high altitude interceptor was developed. It had an armament of two 20mm cannons and one 37mm cannon in an upward position for fighting the B-29 Superfortresses that were bombing the Japanese islands. However, the interceptor variant did not perform well in its new role as it had almost no armor, it lacked self sealing fuel tanks and was slow to climb.","faction":"Japan","type":"fighter","rarity":"Unique","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_dinah_iii","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_dinah_iii_title","SourceString":"Ki-46 DINAH III","LocalizedString":"Ki-46 DINAH III"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":1,"defense":3,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_dinah_iii_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Draw two random 1-cost units from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Draw two random 1-cost units from your deck."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_dinah_iii_history","SourceString":"The Mitsubishi Ki-46, Allied code name “Dinah”,  was a Japanese twin engined reconnaissance aircraft used by the Imperial Japanese Army and Navy air forces during WWII. The aircraft came into service in 1941 and was used before and during the Pacific War, mostly for reconnaissance missions. The Ki-46 was considered a difficult aircraft to counter and only a few were intercepted by Allied pilots. Between 1944-45 a high altitude interceptor was developed. It had an armament of two 20mm cannons and one 37mm cannon in an upward position for fighting the B-29 Superfortresses that were bombing the Japanese islands. However, the interceptor variant did not perform well in its new role as it had almost no armor, it lacked self sealing fuel tanks and was slow to climb.","LocalizedString":"The Mitsubishi Ki-46, Allied code name “Dinah”,  was a Japanese twin engined reconnaissance aircraft used by the Imperial Japanese Army and Navy air forces during WWII. The aircraft came into service in 1941 and was used before and during the Pacific War, mostly for reconnaissance missions. The Ki-46 was considered a difficult aircraft to counter and only a few were intercepted by Allied pilots. Between 1944-45 a high altitude interceptor was developed. It had an armament of two 20mm cannons and one 37mm cannon in an upward position for fighting the B-29 Superfortresses that were bombing the Japanese islands. However, the interceptor variant did not perform well in its new role as it had almost no armor, it lacked self sealing fuel tanks and was slow to climb."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Breakthrough","returnSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/CandidateArtwork/t_ki-46_dinah_iii.t_ki-46_dinah_iii","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/Ki-46_DINAH_III.Ki-46_DINAH_III","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":335.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_dinah_iii_photo","SourceString":"Mitsubishi 